-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Exemption) Order 2008 (S 121/2008), made under s 60 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-exemption-order-2008/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-S121-2008.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- "Part X of the Act" is the name of the ownership-and-control Part in the 2003 and 2012 revised editions; in the 2020 edition it is Part 10 (ss 32 to 45).

§ `Paragraph 2: Exemption`

-- src:6 | 2. —(1) The Minister hereby exempts from Part X of the Act any broadcasting company which holds a Niche Subscription TV Licence granted by the Authority under section 8 of the Act.
@ref para 2(1) (src:6)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the company is a broadcasting company holding a Niche Subscription TV Licence granted by the Authority under section 8 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has revoked the exemption by written notice to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 121/2008 para 2 the company is exempt from Part X of the Act, on` MEANS
    IF `the Exemption Order 2008 as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`the company is a broadcasting company holding a Niche Subscription TV Licence granted by the Authority under section 8 of the Act` AND (NOT `the Minister has revoked the exemption by written notice to the company`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:7 | (2) The Minister may, at any time, revoke the exemption of any broadcasting company under sub-paragraph (1) by written notice to the broadcasting company.
@ref para 2(2) (src:7)
GIVEN `the Minister gives written notice of revocation to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`S 121/2008 para 2(2) the exemption of the company is revoked` MEANS
    IF `the Minister gives written notice of revocation to the company` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
